window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-b82ea2e959edf1ce"]={"zh":"<h1 id=\"mac\">构建 Mac 应用框架</h1> <p>使用 Codex 构建原生 Mac SwiftUI 应用框架，包含侧边栏、详情窗格、检查器、命令和设置。</p> <p>使用 Codex 和 Build macOS Apps 插件，将应用构想变成原生桌面 <code>NavigationSplitView</code> 应用；保持侧边栏选中项稳定，添加菜单、工具栏和键盘快捷键，并将偏好设置放入专门的 <code>Settings</code> 场景。</p> <h2 id=\"_1\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>需要真正桌面应用框架的新 Mac 应用构想，或从 iPad 与 Web 起步、现需加入持久导航、菜单、工具栏和键盘快捷键的项目。</li> <li>侧边栏选择项驱动详情窗格、检查器提供次级元数据或操作的编辑器、资料库、管理或审阅工具。</li> <li>希望将设置放在专门偏好设置窗口中、而不是主内容堆栈中的 Mac 应用。</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"_2\">技能与插件</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>技能或插件</th> <th>用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/build-macos-apps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">build-macos-apps（需联网）</a></td> <td>使用 macOS SwiftUI 模式、窗口管理、AppKit 互操作和构建/运行技能，创建“侧边栏—详情—检查器”布局、接入菜单与设置，并通过以 shell 为先的流程验证应用。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"_3\">技术栈建议</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>需求</th> <th>建议选择</th> <th>原因</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>分栏式应用框架</td> <td><code>NavigationSplitView</code>、<code>.sidebar</code> 列表和 <code>inspector(isPresented:)</code></td> <td>持久侧边栏、详情窗格和检查器，比面向触控的逐页推入式导航更符合常见 Mac 应用布局。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>桌面操作与设置</td> <td><code>commands</code>、<code>CommandMenu</code>、键盘快捷键和 <code>Settings</code> 场景</td> <td>菜单栏操作、快捷键和专门的设置窗口，会让功能更像真正的 Mac 应用，而不是拉伸到桌面上的 iOS 屏幕。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>状态归属</td> <td><code>@State</code>、<code>@SceneStorage</code>、<code>@AppStorage</code> 和显式选中项绑定</td> <td>无需动辄加入视图模型，Codex 也能让侧边栏选中项、检查器可见性和用户偏好保持可预测。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>原生能力补充</td> <td>通过有限的 <code>NSViewRepresentable</code> 或 <code>NSWindow</code> 桥接使用 <a href=\"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/appkit\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">AppKit（需联网）</a></td> <td>仅在 SwiftUI 无法清楚表达某项桌面行为时使用 AppKit，同时仍以 SwiftUI 作为场景与选中状态的唯一事实来源。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"_4\">起步提示词</h2> <p>构建原生 Mac 侧边栏与检查器框架</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">使用 Build macOS Apps 插件，将 [describe your app idea] 转化为原生 Mac SwiftUI 应用框架，其中包括侧边栏、详情窗格、检查器、命令和设置。\n\n约束：\n- 先选择场景模型。主窗口优先使用 `WindowGroup`，并为偏好设置添加专门的 `Settings` 场景。\n- 使用 `NavigationSplitView` 搭建主界面，明确管理选中状态，并使用原生 `.sidebar` 列表、详情界面和用于次级元数据或控件的 `inspector(isPresented:)` 面板。\n- 保持侧边栏行简洁且原生：一个图标、一行标题，最多再加一行简短说明。除非产品确有充分理由，否则不要把每一行都塞进大型自定义卡片。\n- 通过场景级 `commands`、`CommandMenu`、工具栏按钮和键盘快捷键暴露重要操作。不要把执行关键操作的唯一入口藏在手势后面。\n- 使用 `@SceneStorage` 保存窗口范围内的界面状态，使用 `@AppStorage` 保存偏好设置，并用明确由父视图持有的选中项绑定来协调侧边栏与详情内容。\n- 优先使用系统材质、语义颜色和标准侧边栏背景。只有在需要时，才为详情页或检查器里的内容卡片添加自定义样式。\n- 只有当 SwiftUI 无法清楚表达某个具体桌面行为时，才添加范围有限的 AppKit 桥接。\n- 创建或更新 `script/build_and_run.sh`，运行最小但有用的构建/运行检查，并告诉我实际执行的命令。\n\n交付：\n- 场景结构，以及主要的侧边栏、详情页和检查器视图\n- 菜单、工具栏和键盘快捷键的接线方式\n- Settings 场景和偏好设置状态模型\n- 添加的任何 AppKit 桥接，以及它存在的必要原因\n- 构建/运行验证步骤，以及你建议的桌面体验后续改进\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"_5\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/build-macos-apps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Build macOS Apps 插件（需联网）</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23\">代理技能</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>如需完整文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"mac_1\">从 Mac 场景模型开始</h2> <p>本用例旨在把应用构想变成真正为桌面设计、而不是从触控界面堆栈拉伸而来的 Mac 应用框架。请 Codex 先选择场景模型，再围绕稳定的侧边栏选中状态、详情界面，以及用于次级控件或元数据的检查器来设计主窗口。</p> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">原生 Mac 侧边栏与详情应用框架：侧边栏中选中了一个项目，详情窗格显示其内容。 · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/use-cases/macos-sidebar-detail-inspector.png\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>原生 Mac 侧边栏与详情应用框架：侧边栏中选中了一个项目，详情窗格显示其内容。 · <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/use-cases/macos-sidebar-detail-inspector.png\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">打开官网原始媒体</a></figcaption> </figure> <p>如果希望 Codex 采用这种桌面结构，并让构建/运行循环以 shell 为先，请使用 <a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/build-macos-apps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Build macOS Apps 插件（需联网）</a>。其 macOS SwiftUI 模式技能适用于场景设计、侧边栏、检查器、命令、设置，以及当 SwiftUI 还差一点才支持某项 Mac 特定行为时所需的小型 AppKit 桥接。</p> <h2 id=\"_6\">构建侧边栏、详情窗格和检查器</h2> <p>如果某个功能需要持久导航和稳定的选中项，优先使用 <code>NavigationSplitView</code>。侧边栏行应保持原生且简洁，使用系统背景；自定义卡片或密集元数据则留给详情窗格或检查器。</p> <pre><code class=\"language-swift\">struct LibraryRootView: View {\n  @SceneStorage(\"LibraryRootView.selection\") private var selection: Item.ID?\n  @SceneStorage(\"LibraryRootView.showInspector\") private var showInspector = true\n\n  var body: some View {\n    NavigationSplitView {\n      List(selection: $selection) {\n        ForEach(items) { item in\n          Label(item.title, systemImage: item.systemImage)\n            .tag(item.id)\n        }\n      }\n      .listStyle(.sidebar)\n      .navigationTitle(\"Library\")\n    } detail: {\n      ItemDetailView(selection: selection)\n        .inspector(isPresented: $showInspector) {\n          ItemInspectorView(selection: selection)\n        }\n    }\n  }\n}\n</code></pre> <p>如果应用需要不寻常的分栏尺寸、底层窗口协调或自定义响应者链行为，请让 Codex 保持 SwiftUI 框架不变，只为那一个缺口添加最小的 AppKit 桥接。</p> <h2 id=\"_7\">将命令、工具栏和快捷键放在桌面层</h2> <p>Mac 用户应能在菜单栏、工具栏和键盘快捷键中发现重要操作。请 Codex 围绕同一组应用操作接入场景级 <code>commands</code>、与当前上下文相关的菜单项及工具栏按钮，这样桌面用户不必到处寻找只能通过手势触发的控件。</p> <pre><code class=\"language-swift\">@main\nstruct LibraryApp: App {\n  var body: some Scene {\n    WindowGroup {\n      LibraryRootView()\n    }\n    .commands {\n      CommandMenu(\"Library\") {\n        Button(\"New Item\") {\n          // Create a new item.\n        }\n        .keyboardShortcut(\"n\")\n\n        Button(\"Toggle Inspector\") {\n          // Route this command to the focused window or selected item state.\n        }\n        .keyboardShortcut(\"i\", modifiers: [.command, .option])\n      }\n    }\n\n    Settings {\n      LibrarySettingsView()\n    }\n  }\n}\n</code></pre> <p>当命令需要作用于当前详情项时，使用 <code>FocusedValue</code>、场景状态或显式选中状态。如果同一个快捷键会在多个位置注册，请让 Codex 整合其归属，让应用只有一条明确的命令路由。</p> <h2 id=\"settings\">将偏好设置放在 <code>Settings</code> 中</h2> <p>对于应用偏好设置，请使用专门的 <code>Settings</code> 场景，并用 <code>@AppStorage</code> 持久保存用户选择。这通常比在主内容窗口中推入一个设置屏幕更符合 Mac 使用习惯。</p> <pre><code class=\"language-swift\">struct LibrarySettingsView: View {\n  @AppStorage(\"showItemMetadata\") private var showItemMetadata = true\n\n  var body: some View {\n    TabView {\n      Form {\n        Toggle(\"Show Item Metadata\", isOn: $showItemMetadata)\n      }\n      .tabItem { Label(\"General\", systemImage: \"gearshape\") }\n    }\n    .frame(width: 460, height: 260)\n    .scenePadding()\n  }\n}\n</code></pre> <p>如果提示词能说明应用构想、主要内容对象和首要操作，本页的工作流效果最好。先让代理围绕该工作流构建桌面应用框架，再运行小规模的构建/运行检查，并总结场景结构、命令接线、状态归属以及需要桥接的 AppKit 边缘能力。</p> <h2 id=\"_8\">实用建议</h2> <h3 id=\"_9\">保持侧边栏原生简洁</h3> <p>侧边栏行只放一个图标、一行标题，最多再加一行简短说明。将内容更丰富的卡片、计数器和元数据移入详情窗格或检查器，以便快速浏览来源列表。</p> <h3 id=\"_10\">不要把设置藏在主界面堆栈中</h3> <p>如果某项用户偏好影响整个应用，请让 Codex 使用 <code>@AppStorage</code> 将它放进 <code>Settings</code>，并在应用菜单中提供入口，而不是再构建一个逐层推入的设置屏幕。</p> <h3 id=\"appkit\">只在桌面能力有缺口时使用 AppKit</h3> <p>如果功能需要打开/保存面板、第一响应者控制或自定义 <code>NSView</code>，请将 AppKit 作为由 SwiftUI 状态模型负责的小型边缘层，而不要用 AppKit 重写整个窗口。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"build-a-mac-app-shell\">Build a Mac app shell</h1> <p>Use Codex to build a Mac-native SwiftUI app shell with a sidebar, detail pane, inspector, commands, and Settings.</p> <p>Use Codex and the Build macOS Apps plugin to turn an app idea into a desktop-native <code>NavigationSplitView</code> app, keep sidebar selection stable, add menus, toolbars, and keyboard shortcuts, and move preferences into a dedicated <code>Settings</code> scene.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>New Mac app ideas or iPad-first and web-first concepts that need a real desktop shell with persistent navigation, menus, toolbars, and keyboard shortcuts</li> <li>Editor, library, admin, or review tools where a sidebar selection drives a detail pane and an inspector exposes secondary metadata or actions</li> <li>Mac apps where settings should live in a dedicated preferences window instead of another pushed screen in the main content stack</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"skills-plugins\">Skills &amp; Plugins</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Skill or plugin</th> <th>Why use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/build-macos-apps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">build-macos-apps (online)</a></td> <td>Use the macOS SwiftUI patterns, window management, AppKit interop, and build/run skills to create sidebar-detail-inspector layouts, wire menus and settings, and validate the app in a shell-first loop.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"tech-stack-recommendations\">Tech stack recommendations</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Need</th> <th>Good default</th> <th>Why</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Split-view app shell</td> <td><code>NavigationSplitView</code>, <code>.sidebar</code> lists, and <code>inspector(isPresented:)</code></td> <td>A persistent sidebar, detail pane, and inspector match common Mac app layouts better than touch-first push navigation.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Desktop actions and settings</td> <td><code>commands</code>, <code>CommandMenu</code>, keyboard shortcuts, and a <code>Settings</code> scene</td> <td>Menu bar actions, shortcuts, and a dedicated settings window make the feature feel like a real Mac app instead of an iOS screen stretched to desktop.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>State ownership</td> <td><code>@State</code>, <code>@SceneStorage</code>, <code>@AppStorage</code>, and explicit selection bindings</td> <td>Codex can keep sidebar selection, inspector visibility, and user preferences predictable without adding a view model by reflex.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Native escape hatches</td> <td><a href=\"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/appkit\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">AppKit (online)</a> through narrow <code>NSViewRepresentable</code> or <code>NSWindow</code> bridges</td> <td>Use AppKit only for platform behaviors SwiftUI cannot express cleanly, while keeping SwiftUI as the source of truth for scene and selection state.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Build a Mac-Native Sidebar and Inspector Shell</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use the Build macOS Apps plugin to turn [describe your app idea] into a Mac-native SwiftUI app shell with a sidebar, detail pane, inspector, commands, and Settings.\n\nConstraints:\n- Choose the scene model first. Prefer `WindowGroup` for the main window and add a dedicated `Settings` scene for preferences.\n- Build the main UI around `NavigationSplitView` with explicit selection state, a native `.sidebar` list, a detail surface, and an `inspector(isPresented:)` panel for secondary metadata or controls.\n- Keep sidebar rows lightweight and native: one icon, one title line, and at most one short secondary line. Do not wrap every row in large custom cards unless there is a strong product reason.\n- Expose important actions through scene-level `commands`, `CommandMenu`, toolbar buttons, and keyboard shortcuts. Do not hide the only path to a critical action behind gestures.\n- Use `@SceneStorage` for window-scoped UI state, `@AppStorage` for preferences, and explicit parent-owned selection bindings for sidebar/detail coordination.\n- Prefer system materials, semantic colors, and standard sidebar backgrounds. Add custom styling only to detail or inspector content cards when needed.\n- Use a narrow AppKit bridge only if SwiftUI cannot express one specific desktop behavior cleanly.\n- Create or update `script/build_and_run.sh`, run the smallest useful build/run check, and tell me the exact commands you used.\n\nDeliver:\n- the scene structure and main sidebar/detail/inspector views\n- the menu, toolbar, and keyboard shortcut wiring\n- the Settings scene and preference state model\n- any AppKit bridge you added and why it was necessary\n- the build/run validation steps and any desktop UX follow-up you recommend\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/build-macos-apps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Build macOS Apps plugin (online)</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23\">Agent skills</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"start-from-the-mac-scene-model\">Start from the Mac scene model</h2> <p>This use case is for turning an app idea into a Mac app shell that feels built for desktop, not stretched from a touch-first stack. Ask Codex to choose the scene model first, then design the main window around stable sidebar selection, a detail surface, and an inspector for secondary controls or metadata.</p> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">A Mac-native sidebar and detail app shell with a selected item in the sidebar and content in the detail pane · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/use-cases/macos-sidebar-detail-inspector.png\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>A Mac-native sidebar and detail app shell with a selected item in the sidebar and content in the detail pane · <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/use-cases/macos-sidebar-detail-inspector.png\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open original media</a></figcaption> </figure> <p>Use the <a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/build-macos-apps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Build macOS Apps plugin (online)</a> when you want Codex to apply that desktop structure and keep the build/run loop shell-first. Its macOS SwiftUI patterns skill is a good fit for scene design, sidebars, inspectors, commands, settings, and small AppKit bridges when SwiftUI stops just short of one Mac-specific behavior.</p> <h2 id=\"build-a-sidebar-detail-pane-and-inspector\">Build a sidebar, detail pane, and inspector</h2> <p>Prefer <code>NavigationSplitView</code> when the feature benefits from persistent navigation and a stable selected item. Keep sidebar rows native and lightweight, let the sidebar use system backgrounds, and reserve custom cards or dense metadata for the detail pane or inspector.</p> <pre><code class=\"language-swift\">struct LibraryRootView: View {\n  @SceneStorage(\"LibraryRootView.selection\") private var selection: Item.ID?\n  @SceneStorage(\"LibraryRootView.showInspector\") private var showInspector = true\n\n  var body: some View {\n    NavigationSplitView {\n      List(selection: $selection) {\n        ForEach(items) { item in\n          Label(item.title, systemImage: item.systemImage)\n            .tag(item.id)\n        }\n      }\n      .listStyle(.sidebar)\n      .navigationTitle(\"Library\")\n    } detail: {\n      ItemDetailView(selection: selection)\n        .inspector(isPresented: $showInspector) {\n          ItemInspectorView(selection: selection)\n        }\n    }\n  }\n}\n</code></pre> <p>If the app needs unusual split sizing, low-level window coordination, or custom responder-chain behavior, ask Codex to keep the SwiftUI shell intact and add only the smallest AppKit bridge required for that one gap.</p> <h2 id=\"put-commands-toolbars-and-shortcuts-in-the-desktop-layer\">Put commands, toolbars, and shortcuts in the desktop layer</h2> <p>Mac users should be able to discover important actions in the menu bar, the toolbar, and keyboard shortcuts. Ask Codex to wire scene-level <code>commands</code>, context-sensitive menu items, and toolbar buttons around the same app actions so desktop users do not have to hunt for gesture-only controls.</p> <pre><code class=\"language-swift\">@main\nstruct LibraryApp: App {\n  var body: some Scene {\n    WindowGroup {\n      LibraryRootView()\n    }\n    .commands {\n      CommandMenu(\"Library\") {\n        Button(\"New Item\") {\n          // Create a new item.\n        }\n        .keyboardShortcut(\"n\")\n\n        Button(\"Toggle Inspector\") {\n          // Route this command to the focused window or selected item state.\n        }\n        .keyboardShortcut(\"i\", modifiers: [.command, .option])\n      }\n    }\n\n    Settings {\n      LibrarySettingsView()\n    }\n  }\n}\n</code></pre> <p>Use <code>FocusedValue</code>, scene state, or explicit selection state when a command should apply to the current detail item. If a shortcut would be registered in multiple places, ask Codex to consolidate ownership so the app has one clear command route.</p> <h2 id=\"keep-preferences-in-settings\">Keep preferences in <code>Settings</code></h2> <p>For app preferences, use a dedicated <code>Settings</code> scene and persist durable user choices with <code>@AppStorage</code>. This is usually a better Mac fit than pushing a settings screen inside the main content window.</p> <pre><code class=\"language-swift\">struct LibrarySettingsView: View {\n  @AppStorage(\"showItemMetadata\") private var showItemMetadata = true\n\n  var body: some View {\n    TabView {\n      Form {\n        Toggle(\"Show Item Metadata\", isOn: $showItemMetadata)\n      }\n      .tabItem { Label(\"General\", systemImage: \"gearshape\") }\n    }\n    .frame(width: 460, height: 260)\n    .scenePadding()\n  }\n}\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"prompt-the-app-concept-then-validate-the-shell\">Prompt the app concept, then validate the shell</h2> <p>This page works best when your prompt names the app concept, the main content objects, and the primary actions, then asks Codex to build the desktop shell around that workflow first. Have the agent run a small build/run check and summarize the scene structure, command wiring, state ownership, and any AppKit edge it had to bridge.</p> <h2 id=\"practical-tips\">Practical tips</h2> <h3 id=\"keep-the-sidebar-native\">Keep the sidebar native</h3> <p>Use one icon, one title line, and at most one short secondary line in sidebar rows. Move richer cards, counters, and metadata into the detail pane or inspector so the source list stays easy to scan.</p> <h3 id=\"avoid-hiding-settings-in-the-main-stack\">Avoid hiding settings in the main stack</h3> <p>If a user preference affects the whole app, ask Codex to put that control in <code>Settings</code> with <code>@AppStorage</code> and expose an entry point through the app menu instead of building another pushed settings screen.</p> <h3 id=\"save-appkit-for-narrow-desktop-gaps\">Save AppKit for narrow desktop gaps</h3> <p>If the feature needs open/save panels, first-responder control, or a custom <code>NSView</code>, use AppKit as a small edge around a SwiftUI-owned state model rather than rewriting the whole window in AppKit.</p>"};
